              {
                "type": "text",
                "props": {
                  "text": "### Derivative Rules\n\nThe derivative is the instantaneous rate of change, the slope of the tangent."
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "table",
                "props": {
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "RULE",
                      "FORMULA"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Power",
                      "`d/dx x^n = n*x^(n-1)`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Product",
                      "`(fg)' = f'g + fg'`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Quotient",
                      "`(f/g)' = (f'g - fg')/g^2`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Chain",
                      "`(f(g(x)))' = f'(g(x)) * g'(x)`"
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "props": {
                  "text": "> **Example.** `d/dx (3x+1)^5 = 5(3x+1)^4 * 3 = 15(3x+1)^4` (chain). Quotient mnemonic: low d-high minus high d-low, over low squared."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "tags": [
              "calculus"
            ],
            "w": 6,
            "slots": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "props": {
                  "text": "### Key Derivatives\n\nMemorize these cold. They appear in almost every problem."
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "table",
                "props": {
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "f(x)",
                      "f'(x)"
                    ],
                    [
                      "`e^x`",
                      "`e^x`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "`ln x`",
                      "`1/x`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "`sin x`",
                      "`cos x`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "`cos x`",
                      "`-sin x`"
                    ],
                    [
                      "`tan x`",
                      "`sec^2 x`"
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "props": {
                  "text": "> **Example.** `d/dx ln(x^2+1) = 2x/(x^2+1)` (chain with ln). $e^x$ is the only function that is its own derivative, up to scale."
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
